  "goodToKnow": "Die Dreharbeiten (plural only) means the filming or shoot of a film or series. Einen Film drehen means to shoot a film, from the hand-cranked cameras of the early days. Das Drehbuch is the screenplay, der Drehort the location, and der Drehtag a shooting day. Studio Babelsberg near Potsdam, founded in 1912, is one of the oldest large film studios in the world, where Metropolis was filmed."
